      "name": "Bristol Supertram",
      "status": "abandoned",
      "description": "Line One of a light rail scheme backed by the government in 2001: 16 stops over about 17 km from Union Street in the centre via Temple Meads, reopened stations on the Filton Bank line and Bristol Parkway to Aztec West, with an extension proposed to MoD Abbey Wood and UWE. South Gloucestershire withdrew over a Cribbs Causeway extension, and Bristol City Council cancelled the scheme in March 2004.",
