    "mass-transit": {
      "name": "Bristol underground mass transit",
      "status": "proposed",
      "description": "Four radial routes from Temple Meads studied for the West of England Combined Authority and made public in November 2022: south to the airport, north to Aztec West and Almondsbury, north-east to the Science Park and south-east to Keynsham, each with an underground option (about £4.5 billion in all). Shown here as the underground options; the scheme remains at feasibility stage.",
